# Write paths

A *write path* gives us the ability to create a new deep copy of complex of objects, overwriting only selected slots. Some of which are a way down the object hierarchy.


`[:Class | path = expr]` rebuilds only the objects explicitly on the path.


In this example we build a World from a number of deeply nested objects and create methods that update some of the properties. For example, the Fountain sits six levels down but can still have its name or number of jets updated without disrupting the rest of the structure.


Type a command and press Enter: 
* `jets` updates the number of jets
* `rain` makes the ocean deeper
* `drought` evaporates water from the ocean and reduces the number of jets
* or a new fountain name.


## Schema

```
World = Continent Ocean
Continent = Country
Country = Capital
Capital = Plaza
Plaza = Fountain
Fountain = Int/jets String/name
Ocean = Int/depth
```

## Construction

```
[:World
  [:Continent
    [:Country
      [:Capital
        [:Plaza
          [:Fountain 7 "Triton"]]]]]
  [:Ocean 4000]
]
```

## Methods

```
Fountain::rename = { String/n | [:Fountain | name = n] }

World::moreJets = {
  [:World | continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.jets = (continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.jets + 1)]
}

World::renameFountain = { String/n |
  [:World | continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.name = n]
}

World::rain = {
  [:World | ocean.depth = (ocean.depth + 100)]
}

World::drought = {
  [:World | continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.jets = 1, ocean.depth = 1000]
}

World::command = { String/line |
  switch (line)
    "jets" -> { this.moreJets() }
    "rain" -> { this.rain() }
    "drought" -> { this.drought() }
    else -> { if (line == "") { this } else { this.renameFountain(line) } }
}


World::label = {
  f = continent.country.capital.plaza.fountain.
  jets = f.jets.
  depth = ocean.depth.
  "Fountain {name} has {jets} jets; ocean {depth} deep.".tpl({String:String "name": f.name, "jets": jets.str(), "depth": depth.str()})
}
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var world = WorldAssemblage.factory();
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    trace(world.toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("moreJets");
    trace(world.moreJets().toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("renameFountain");
    trace(world.renameFountain("Arethusa").toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("rain");
    trace(world.rain().toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("drought");
    trace(world.drought().toConstruction(0, helper));
}
```
